* fix(bots): room status is read per thread, and a parked member reads unavailable

Outcomes and the round strip keyed on the newest user message in the whole room, so posting in
thread B turned a failed member from thread A idle and the strip showed B's round while A worked.
Each turn now counts against its own thread's current discussion, and the round comes from the
live tasks' round_index (the thread being replied in first, else whichever thread works), with
the old guess kept for gateways that send no round_index.

The per-member unavailable signal is turn.deferred with reason member_unavailable; the room-level
member.unavailable names no member and stays a room notice in the history.

The handoff scan was quadratic in the log and re-ran on every poll: it is one pass now, and the
workspace keeps the log array's identity while its length and last seq are unchanged.

* fix(bots): a closed room drops its Bots-list glyph; held replies keep their thread

publishCanonicalRoomLive had no cleanup, so a room closed while working or awaiting approval kept
that glyph for the session. Each open workspace now holds the entry and the last one to unmount
