* feat(bots): cron jobs post into Group Chats; rooms get a purpose and shared notes

A scheduled job can now deliver to a Bot Mode Group Chat with
`deliver: room:<room_id>[@<profile>]`. The output lands as one message in
the room, labelled with the job's name. It starts a round only for the
members it @mentions (`@all` addresses everyone); without a mention it is
just a message in the room, so a feed of scheduled results never makes
every Bot answer it. Failure notices never start a round. The post is an
ordinary `message.user` event with a server-minted `cron:<job>` actor, so
the existing thread/round machinery and replay stay unchanged and a client
cannot impersonate a job.

Rooms also gain a short purpose and a small shared notes block
(`groups.context`, shown and edited in the room header's Room settings).
Both are rendered at the top of each member's turn prompt, which is the
user-role message, never the system prompt, so prompt caching is
untouched. They are stored as `room.context_set` events in the room log
and read as of the message that opened a discussion: the planner stays a
pure function of the log, and an edit mid-discussion never re-plans a turn
already admitted (it applies from the next message). Rooms without a
purpose keep byte-identical prompts.

* fix(cron): catch only room-store errors in Group Chat delivery

* fix(cron): post to the room copy a worker actually serves

The shared-store import copies rooms out of state.db into shared-state.db without deleting the
