interpreter runs counts now.

* ci(tests-os): bound the PowerShell warm-up step at 3 minutes

* fix(runner): a forked file is a main process to multiprocessing; review cleanups

Under the fork server multiprocessing still saw each file as the server's
child: current_process() was ForkServerProcess-N with a parent, every file
after the first inherited the runner's /tmp/pymp-* temp dir, and __main__ was
this runner, re-run in every child as __mp_main__ (~7-20ms per file). A
test's own Process, Pool or spawn context now sees what python -m pytest gives
it: a parentless MainProcess, a temp dir under its TMPDIR, and pytest as
__main__ and __mp_main__; the server preloads the runner once. The fork probe
compares these against a fresh pytest process, from the server's second child.

Also from review: run_tests_fork_child.run takes keyword arguments and one
argv; the start-under-lock is one helper the race test calls, and the test
starts 2000 children (unlocked, ~1 status in 400 comes back 255), so dropping
either lock fails it; kill() leaves a reaped pid alone; the output file is
removed when start() fails; the exit-status note skips exit 1 (tests failed,
already reported) and crashes; the 2.0s default duration is one constant; the
new tests reuse the file's runner helpers. The docstring records the gap left:
a daemon a test forks without exec escapes the leftover sweep.

* refactor(runner): both ways to start a file live in run_tests_launch.py

Review: the fork mode spread its server state, lock, process creation and
process-group rules through the runner, so _run_one_file_once had to know that
a forked child calls setsid() while a subprocess needs getpgid(). The runner
now calls start_pytest() and gets the process and its group back; the fork
server, its lock and the Popen shim live with it. Behaviour is unchanged.

classify_changes lists the launch module and the fork child as test harness
next to run_tests_parallel.py, so editing either starts the lanes a runner
edit starts (the fork child was missing since it was added).

* test(runner): a forked file's own spawn and default-context workers work

Review: the fork probe compared multiprocessing names and fields but never
