* fix(desktop): isolate reused tool_call_id from prior lost-completion row

* fix(desktop): gate reused tool_call_id re-arm on per-row in-flight evidence

Address review feedback on the running-phase re-arm: the running-phase
gate in `toolCallOwnerMessageId` consulted the session-wide
`interimBoundaryPending` flag as ownership evidence for a sealed-no-result
part, but that flag is raised by the CURRENT turn's interim boundary and
can belong to a different bubble than the candidate row. A new turn that
emits `message.start` -> `message.interim` -> `tool.start` (reusing an id
from a prior, lost-completion turn) therefore re-armed the prior turn's
sealed history and clobbered it, leaving the new turn without a row of its
own.

Drop the `session` parameter and the session-global term so the
running-phase gate re-arms only when the owning message itself is still in
flight (`pending` or `interim`) — the interim-boundary and mid-turn-user-
message paths that re-arm a sealed part seal the bubble in place and mark
that same message `interim`, so the evidence lives on the candidate row.
The `complete`-phase #113035 late-completion reconciliation is unchanged
(this call site only ever passes 'complete').

Add a RED witness reproducing the cross-turn hole: turn A loses its
completion and settles; turn B raises `interimBoundaryPending` via
`message.interim` and then reuses the id. The witness fails on the
session-global gate (one clobbered row, `expected length 2 but got 1`)
and passes with the per-row gate (two rows: A intact and sealed without a
result, B with its own command and result). The existing mid-turn
mid-turn-user-message re-attach and the #113035 pure-settle late-
completion guards stay green.

* test(desktop): cover Stop and optimistic send tool-id reuse boundaries

* test(desktop): follow main's Stop and send finalizers in the reuse tests

