* fix(desktop): draw a re-delivered tool event for a finished call once

Only an unresolved tool part can own a lifecycle event, so a second copy of
a start or completion for a call that had already returned landed in the
live bubble as a brand-new row. A background delegate_task returns in about
a second, so a re-delivery showed the whole fan-out twice: "5 Subagents" in
the status stack over ten delegate rows in the transcript.

A copy of a call this turn already finished (same id and name, and the same
arguments for a start or the same result for a completion) now leaves the
transcript untouched. Constant-id providers and a later turn reusing an id
with the same arguments still get their own rows.

* fix(desktop): route a tool start that arrives after the turn settled like a late completion

The reuse fix routes a running event to a sealed, result-less row only while
that row's message is still in flight. A copy of a start that arrives after
the turn settled, while its completion is still outstanding, therefore found
no owner. It seeded a fresh pending bubble under the finished turn, and the
late completion then attached to that new row instead of the sealed one.

With no turn live, a running event can only be a late or repeated frame of a
call already on screen, so route it by the completion rule. A turn that is
live keeps the reuse rule, so a new turn reusing an id still gets its own row.

