* [daveey] fix(cron): release a quota hold once its refusing pool serves again

x-reply-discovery (hub ac8b62d38a0b) was parked until 2026-11-04T15:07Z by the 11-02 22:07Z
SubscriptionQuotaUnavailable openai-codex/gpt-6-astra refusal, while the same pool served sibling
cron sessions (bsky-reply-discovery) all of 11-03; ~26 in-window slots were skipped.

Five whys:
1. Job not firing -> next_run_at parked at quota_hold_until 11-04 15:07Z.
2. Park computed from the pool refusal's resets_at (min over exhausted OAuth entries at refusal).
3. Pool reopened long before that (another entry/cooldown cleared): resets_at is an upper bound.
4. cron/quota_hold.py held one-way: only a run of the SAME job reaching the model cleared it,
   and the hold prevented that run.
Root (happened): no early-release check against current local pool state.
Root (not caught): no test for "pool recovers before resets_at".

Fix:
- plan_hold stamps the refusing route (quota_hold_route {provider, model}) from the typed
  refusal (SubscriptionQuotaUnavailable .provider/.model; fallback chain: terminal route),
  carried run -> bookkeeping via the _quota_hold_route RUN_JOB_FLAG.
- The due scan, for a cron job with an active hold, a known route and no queued run-now,
  consults that route's local OAuth pool (load_pool + quota_unavailable + has_available; no
  network). When serving it clears the hold and moves next_run_at to the schedule's NEXT natural
  occurrence (never an immediate catch-up fire) and logs "quota hold released early: pool
  serving". A pool read fault keeps the hold.
- Holds planned before the stamp existed release only when their persisted last_error is the
  exact SubscriptionQuotaUnavailable message (which names the route) AND the pool check agrees;
  text never parks a job. Holds naming no route, interval holds, and holds whose next natural
  slot is not earlier than the parked instant are unchanged. Caps/allocation untouched.

Tests: tests/cron/test_quota_hold_early_release.py (RED on base: 9/10 fail; the legacy-unchanged
control passes on both), plus existing test_quota_hold*.py.

