* [daveey] fix(routing): a router-picked pin is not David's pin; a far quota wall reroutes it in-class

Problem: MacBook Desktop chat 20261026_000514_23ef49 went dead for ~33 h from 11-02 13:59 PT. Every
turn failed before it started with "Subscription quota unavailable for openai-codex/gpt-6-astra;
resets at 1793774268" while claude-opus-5-5 in the same `deep` class was available.

Why 1: the turn's pre-build lookup raised the wall (run_turn_runner → runtime_provider →
       model_routing_runtime.resolve_class_runtime).
Why 2: a concrete model resolves through pin_policy, which keeps one route, so Opus was never tried.
Why 3: the router picked Astra; the gateway's concrete echo of that pick made RoutingState._allocate
       upgrade the allocation to exact_pin, and exact pins refuse failover.
Why 4: routes did not record where a pin came from: a router pick, the config default and a model
       David named all stored exact_pin (MacBook: 9017 deep allocation+exact rows vs 2 switches;
       hub: 4622 vs 13).
Root (happened): pin provenance was not recorded, so router picks were treated as David's choices.
Root (not caught): no test covered "an allocation echoed as a concrete model, then walled", and the
       refusal named an epoch timestamp, so nothing told David the chat was parked or how to leave.

Fix:
- model_routing_state: every new route records `pin_source` (`explicit` = honoured switch or a model
  David named; `default` = router pick, config default). An echo never upgrades an allocation to
  exact. Legacy rows count as explicit only when they record `explicit-switch`.
- model_routing_walls (new) + resolve_managed_runtime: a `default` pin whose subscription wall resets
  6 h or more away is re-selected in its class (`same-class-failover`, `walled_from` recorded), and
  the session then follows its reroute even though its stored model still names the walled one.
  Explicit pins, Kanban card pins (t_01a19990897b9d9b owns those) and walls under 6 h still hold.
- gateway: the pre-build lookup knows the turn's session (`routing_session`) and defers a reroutable
  wall to the agent build instead of refusing; the chat gets one line ("<model> quota is out until
  <PT>; continuing on <model>."). A held pin's reply names the PT reset and /model.
- Detection: WARNING `routing: walled default pin rerouted <from>→<to> until <reset>`, once per
  episode.

Tests: tests/agent/test_walled_default_pin.py (red on 9825be18561: 6 failed, 4 controls passed);
test_model_routing_state_contention's upgrade assertion now asserts the echo stays non-exact.

Undo: revert this commit; older code ignores `pin_source`/`walled_from`, no migration.
